## Build the Tallest Tower

**Materials Needed:**
- A set of wooden blocks of various shapes
- Measuring tape

**Instructions:**
1. Invite the children to build the tallest tower they can without it falling over.
2. Ask them to predict how many blocks tall their tower will be.
3. Once completed, measure the tower together using both standard (measuring tape) and non-standard (e.g., hands) units.
4. Discuss why certain shapes (like cubes) work better at the bottom than others (like cones).
