## Why Spatial Reasoning Matters

Spatial reasoning in early childhood is a strong predictor of later mathematical achievement. 

When children engage in block play, they are experimenting with structural integrity, balance, and geometry. According to research by *Clements and Sarama (2009)*, playful exploration of 3D objects allows children to develop mental models of spatial relationships. 

**Key Takeaways for Teachers:**
- Allow for unstructured building time.
- Introduce spatial vocabulary during play (*above, below, next to, base, solid*).
- Encourage children to draw their structures after building them to bridge 3D to 2D representations.
